{
    "background_story": "In the dense rainforest, a flock of brood parasites thrived, laying their eggs in the nests of unsuspecting hosts. Jadiel, a cuckoo bird, was notorious for her cunning and ruthless tactics. She would often sneak into the nests of other birds, removing their eggs and replacing them with her own. But Jadiel's most heinous behavior was her practice of infanticide. When she discovered that a host bird had recognized her egg and was about to eject it, she would attack the nest, killing the host's own chicks to ensure the survival of her own offspring. The other birds in the forest feared and avoided Jadiel, whispering warnings to each other about the 'child-killer'. Her actions were a grim reminder of the harsh realities of the natural world, where survival often came at the expense of others.",
